# Replication of metadata: checked spec

A codebase replicates as bundles of content-addressed objects (D60, D91). Metadata (doc comments,
comments, attributes, spec prose, inferred schemes) is not hashed, so a change to it alone made no
object: a push sent metadata only with objects the remote lacked, and an import kept the first
metadata it saw (task f4afc2c0). A clone of the R2 remote printed spec prose under the wrong blocks.

Now each commit records a metadata snapshot, a tree of objects keyed by hash prefix that the history
node names, so a metadata change is an object that replicates and compacts like any other
([D134](../../docs/DECISIONS.md)). A fast-forward writes the snapshot of the new head; a merge merges
the snapshots hash by hash. Written in the order of the process (D92): requirements, then APIs and
laws, then the implementation; the laws ran red against stubs.

## Extensions

| Term | URI |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: metadata snapshots
  signatures:
  - Codebase.recordMetas : Text -> Map Text Entry -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.putMetas : Text -> Text -> List (Text, Sexp) -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.readMetas : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text Sexp
  - Codebase.mergeMetas : Map Text Sexp -> Map Text Sexp -> Map Text Sexp -> Map Text Sexp
  - Codebase.applyMetas : Text -> Map Text Sexp -> {IO} List Text
```

## Requirements

```mdl
req R-1: a commit that changes only metadata is a new history node, and its snapshot holds the new metadata
  by: Replicate.Spec.commitRecordsMetas
```

```mdl
req R-2: a store that pulls a metadata-only change and fast-forwards to it holds the new metadata
  by: Replicate.Spec.cloneGetsMetadataChange
```

```mdl
req R-3: a merge of concurrent work takes the side that changed a hash's metadata, and merges two changes as the store does
  by: Replicate.Spec.concurrentMetadataMerges | Replicate.Spec.theirsWhereOursUnchanged | Replicate.Spec.oursWhereTheirsUnchanged | Replicate.Spec.bothChangedMerge
```

```mdl
req R-4: a metadata snapshot travels in the bundles a push writes, as the objects it is made of
  by: Replicate.Spec.closureHoldsMetas
```

## Theorems

The laws are the definitions under `Replicate.Spec`: `deus ls Replicate.Spec.` lists them and `deus view` prints them.
